atchet, correct?", "\"Yes, a shovel, and {V} swung it toward me first. I raised the hatchet to block, and the blow landed in a way I will regret for life.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} died on the driveway from a single chest wound after an argument with a neighbor, {D}, over a fallen tree. A neighbor saw {D} walk away holding a hatchet, and a bloody hatchet was in {D}'s shed. The State will show the hatchet and the autopsy.", "Jurors will also see a neighbor who saw {V} raise a shovel, a swing made in fear, and no weapon brought to the fight. {D} protected {D.himself}."),
